<% content_for :title, "#{t("marketing.footer.privacy")} – Hutba" %>

<section class="legal">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1><%= t("marketing.footer.privacy") %></h1>

    <%# TODO: have this reviewed before launch. It describes what the app actually does today. %>
    <p>[Draft – to be completed before launch.]</p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>[Company name] d.o.o., [address]. Email: <%= mail_to Rails.configuration.x.contact_email %></p>

    <h2>Live translation</h2>
    <p>During a broadcast, the imam's audio is sent to our speech recognition and translation provider (Soniox) and the translated text is shown to listeners. Neither audio nor text is recorded or stored by us.</p>

    <h2>Listeners</h2>
    <p>Listeners do not create an account. We store anonymous connection statistics (time, language, duration) to show mosques how many people read along.</p>

    <h2>Mosque accounts</h2>
    <p>For mosque accounts we store the mosque name, contact person, email address and billing details needed to provide the service. When a mosque signs up we also store how it found us: the optional answer from the signup form, the campaign tag of the link it came through (e.g. a flyer QR code) and the name of the website it came from. These are kept in the session cookie until signup and are not shared with anyone.</p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>We only use a technically necessary session cookie. There is no tracking across websites, no analytics service and no advertising cookies.</p>
  </div>
</section>
